                    "name": "b84330808"
                },
                "message": "Infer the result type of C++ operator overloads in binary operations\n\nInferring the type of an untyped variable that is reassigned from a C++\nbinary operation, e.g. `it += 1` on a vector iterator, crashed the\ncompiler because the binop inferred no type. Use the matching operator\noverload for the inferred type, and fall back to a Python object instead\nof crashing when no type can be inferred.\n\nCloses #7527",
